WEBVTT

00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:14,670
I'm experiencing pain in my spine at the location where I had surgery.

00:00:14,670 --> 00:00:18,830
Could this be part of the healing process or a side of the disease?

00:00:18,830 --> 00:00:22,670
The answer is yes, could be either.

00:00:22,670 --> 00:00:31,550
The only way to only know if it's metastasized to that area is a PET scan,

00:00:31,550 --> 00:00:37,150
or a CT scan would see that too.

00:00:37,230 --> 00:00:42,510
It's, but it can be healing too.

00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:46,830
So as you're healing from an injury, you're going to have pain.

00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:50,830
So I know we said this before, whatever we have cancer,

00:00:52,030 --> 00:00:54,990
any pain or any symptom, we go, oh, it's getting worse.

00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:57,710
But that may be true, but it's not always true.

00:00:57,710 --> 00:01:00,030
So we just got to be careful not to go there mentally.

00:01:01,710 --> 00:01:05,710
The only way to know for sure is to do a scan to see what's going on.

00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:11,150
So if the pain is excruciated and it's, you know,

00:01:11,150 --> 00:01:15,630
that's another way to know if that, if the pain is unbearable,

00:01:15,630 --> 00:01:18,990
it's very high at a scale of 1 to 10, that's not normal.

00:01:19,710 --> 00:01:21,630
Is that normal, a healing pain?

00:01:21,630 --> 00:01:28,350
Then I would definitely talk to the doctor about that.

